Magenta.js's audio utilities are based on google/web-audio-recognition (librosa-compat), also Apache-2.0.

Changes made by the Pauta authors (2026), as required by section 4(b) of the license: the model graph is rewritten with
core TensorFlow.js ops instead of tfjs-layers (BatchNorm folded into the convolutions, fused activations, an LSTM with
a fused WebGL cell), the input is processed chunk by chunk with the same context frames and carried LSTM state, the log
mel front end is reimplemented for speed with the same arithmetic, and the decoder outputs the app's NoteEvent. Every
derived file keeps the original copyright header and states its changes.

Paper: Curtis Hawthorne, Erich Elsen, Jialin Song, Adam Roberts, Ian Simon, Colin Raffel, Jesse Engel, Sageev Oore,
Douglas Eck. "Onsets and Frames: Dual-Objective Piano Transcription." ISMIR 2018.

The model weights are not in this folder: see public/models/onsets-frames/NOTICE.
